From 6ff35e21a36de19a9c9abd27c9f7b42b3a920239 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tuth <tuth3378@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:11:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/24] MS2000: H-bank program change crash - root cause +
 4-layer JIT hardening

MEASURED ROOT CAUSE (one defect, three costumes):
- H08->H09 program change in the H bank sends the DSP PC to 0x800010 (bit 23
  set), outside the JIT-covered program window (mem.sizeP()). The JIT indexes
  the block cache / funcs tables with the raw PC:
  * ORIGINAL upstream code: funcCreate -> create(pc, true) -> exec(pc) nests
    one C++ frame per first-time block; a first-time linear run nests ~4000
    deep -> STACK OVERFLOW inside asmjit (measured depth 3951, VEH frame
    chain funcCreate->create->emit->optimize->constantFolding->areFlagsLive).
    This kills the host (VSTHost/DAW crash on H10-H14 vocoder program change).
  * Nesting removed but block never run: dispatcher spins re-calling the
    create thunk -> 26 GB commit growth -> Windows Event 1003 resource
    exhaustion -> the whole machine freezes (measured twice, 06:29 and 10:05).
  * With bounded retry: std::bad_alloc thrown through noexcept funcCreate ->
    std::terminate -> abort() 0xC0000409 (measured, named via try/catch
    instrumentation on stderr: "[JIT-EXC] funcCreate std::exception at pc
    0x800010: bad allocation").

FIX (all four dispatch/compile choke points bounds-checked against
memory().sizeP(); an out-of-window PC never indexes any table again):
1. jittrampoline.cpp: the generated execUntilCycles loop cmp pc,sizeP /
   jae exit before loading the entries pointer - never OOB-read a function
   pointer (the old code could call garbage from past the table).
2. jit.cpp funcCreate: window check, rate-limited stderr log, return.
3. jit.cpp funcRecreate: same.
4. dsp.h execOneEnsureRun: same before touching m_jitEntries.

NESTING FIX (upstream-able, CPU flat, HW semantics kept):
- create() no longer execs from inside funcCreate/funcRecreate: one C++ frame
  per first-time block is gone; the dispatch loop picks the fresh block up.
- execOneEnsureRun (dsp.cpp execInterrupt + dsp.h execJit): one-shot callers
  re-read the entry after a create-thunk call and run the fresh block on a
  flat stack, bounded 16 retries - an ISR is never silently skipped.
- makeRoomForFirstInstruction failure path now logs (rate-limited) instead
  of returning silently.

VERIFIED (headless bankstorm, warden-guarded):
- build green; boot passes (status t=2.52 s, pads at t=6.002/6.502, H08
  program change completes: H01:Poly400 -> H08:Pulse Comp).
- no STACK OVERFLOW, no std::terminate, no bad_alloc until the (pre-existing,
  upstream) JIT memory appetite crosses the warden ceiling - the watchdog
  kills the process and the machine stays healthy. NOTE: the 4+ GB growth
  during boot/storm is a separate, pre-existing upstream defect (Event 1003
  fired during the ORIGINAL code too, 06:29:46) - next hunt.
